1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,694
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,696 --> 00:00:03,011
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:04,031 --> 00:00:05,976
(Episode 16)

4
00:00:19,075 --> 00:00:20,075
(Audio Story Listening Booth Registration)

5
00:00:31,372 --> 00:00:34,085
- Do you need some help?
- Yes, please.

6
00:01:07,371 --> 00:01:09,394
You can turn it on here.

7
00:01:09,482 --> 00:01:11,478
There it is. Thank you.

8
00:01:28,712 --> 00:01:29,726
Sorry?

9
00:01:30,294 --> 00:01:31,785
You seem interested in children's stories.

10
00:01:31,787 --> 00:01:33,346
Do you work for a publishing company?

11
00:01:34,519 --> 00:01:35,551
No.

12
00:01:36,452 --> 00:01:39,128
I came because I'm interested in
children's book illustrations.

13
00:01:39,758 --> 00:01:42,039
There are lots of good books
in the back too.

14
00:01:42,429 --> 00:01:43,773
I was just about to go there.

15
00:01:44,372 --> 00:01:45,820
Enjoy looking around.

16
00:01:58,665 --> 00:01:59,681
Listen to this.

17
00:02:00,255 --> 00:02:01,291
Okay.

18
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:12,816
- Here, like this.
- Okay.

19
00:02:16,169 --> 00:02:17,391
I can hear it now.

20
00:02:26,863 --> 00:02:29,476
- Welcome home.
- I'm starving.

21
00:02:29,625 --> 00:02:31,463
Dinner's ready.

22
00:02:35,266 --> 00:02:37,478
What's all this?

23
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,760
Did you buy all these?

24
00:02:40,761 --> 00:02:42,589
Yeah. They're really fun and well-made.

25
00:02:42,592 --> 00:02:44,736
I brought them home to show you.

26
00:02:44,738 --> 00:02:46,071
You should take a look too.

27
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,306
Seriously...

28
00:02:48,412 --> 00:02:51,298
He really is planning to expand
the publishing house.

29
00:02:52,018 --> 00:02:54,002
I don't know what's gotten into him.

30
00:02:54,004 --> 00:02:56,383
He's been smiling all day.

31
00:02:57,779 --> 00:03:00,010
- Is father home?
- Look at this.

32
00:03:00,338 --> 00:03:02,705
Looks like he cleared out
the entire bookstore.

33
00:03:08,164 --> 00:03:09,501
The illustrations are beautiful.

34
00:03:09,668 --> 00:03:10,808
Right?

35
00:03:11,269 --> 00:03:12,728
The stories are fun too.

36
00:03:12,805 --> 00:03:13,814
Honey,

37
00:03:13,848 --> 00:03:16,292
wouldn't it be great
if we'd been born now?

38
00:03:16,372 --> 00:03:18,098
What did we have back then?
"Kongjwi and Patjwi?"

39
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,738
- What else?
- "Galaxy Express 999?"

40
00:03:21,741 --> 00:03:23,703
Are you from that generation?

41
00:03:23,705 --> 00:03:26,700
- "Galaxy Express 999" is great.
- It is, actually.

42
00:03:28,392 --> 00:03:30,416
Father, you must feel rich today.

43
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:32,005
Of course. So you know the feeling?

44
00:03:32,098 --> 00:03:35,198
Buying books costs money,
but it still makes you feel richer.

45
00:03:36,098 --> 00:03:37,318
Nonsense.

46
00:03:40,298 --> 00:03:43,526
- Sir, we're heading downstairs.
- Okay. Good work today.

47
00:03:47,878 --> 00:03:49,870
If she hadn't helped me,
I might not have made it inside.

48
00:03:49,932 --> 00:03:51,118
I need to learn that too.

49
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:53,614
It's such a relief when someone helps
at a time like that.

50
00:03:53,617 --> 00:03:56,483
Exactly. Everything changes
so quickly these days.

51
00:03:56,485 --> 00:03:58,546
Are you really going to focus
only on the publishing house?

52
00:03:58,925 --> 00:04:01,332
Running the publishing house alone
will keep me busy enough.

53
00:04:01,412 --> 00:04:04,212
The young woman I met today
was interested in children's books.

54
00:04:04,625 --> 00:04:07,105
I asked if she worked for a publisher,
but she didn't answer.

55
00:04:07,525 --> 00:04:09,255
I was going to ask her to work for us,

56
00:04:09,257 --> 00:04:11,382
but I didn't want her thinking
I was some weird old man.

57
00:04:11,384 --> 00:04:12,523
Good call.

58
00:04:12,525 --> 00:04:14,064
Watch what you say, Father.

59
00:04:14,066 --> 00:04:16,947
She was sweet and pretty,
though not as pretty as Do Hee.

60
00:04:17,158 --> 00:04:19,357
Come to think of it,
Do Hee hasn't been around much.

61
00:04:19,778 --> 00:04:21,103
Tell her to come by more often.

62
00:04:21,676 --> 00:04:22,691
Okay.

63
00:04:25,956 --> 00:04:28,050
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

64
00:04:29,165 --> 00:04:31,588
- O Reum.
- Grandma.

65
00:04:32,983 --> 00:04:36,885
I'm sorry. I should've been here
for you yesterday.

66
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:38,848
You missed Jonduki, didn't you?

67
00:04:38,850 --> 00:04:43,176
- Yeah. Jonduki isn't sick.
- That's right.

68
00:04:43,178 --> 00:04:45,196
Jonduki isn't sick.

69
00:04:45,198 --> 00:04:46,368
Sweetheart.

70
00:04:46,485 --> 00:04:49,796
- Was yesterday hard? Did you cry a lot?
- Yeah.

71
00:04:49,798 --> 00:04:54,898
- I cried.
- You did? Poor baby.

72
00:04:54,958 --> 00:04:57,557
Why didn't you come, Grandma?

73
00:04:57,998 --> 00:04:59,821
Grandma...

74
00:04:59,885 --> 00:05:02,518
had to go to class.

75
00:05:02,838 --> 00:05:05,237
And when you cry,

76
00:05:05,239 --> 00:05:07,416
I cry too.

77
00:05:07,422 --> 00:05:09,901
Mom cried too.

78
00:05:10,029 --> 00:05:14,057
She did? You need to get well soon.

79
00:05:14,358 --> 00:05:15,763
Sweetheart.

80
00:05:16,518 --> 00:05:18,080
What are we going to do?

81
00:05:23,572 --> 00:05:26,337
- Did you two discuss this?
- Yes.

82
00:05:26,778 --> 00:05:28,766
Please sign and stamp here.

83
00:05:28,768 --> 00:05:30,989
You have the documents
I told you about, right?

84
00:05:34,258 --> 00:05:37,065
We'll process everything
and contact you again.

85
00:05:45,145 --> 00:05:47,149
- You won't regret this?
- No.

86
00:05:48,865 --> 00:05:51,303
Don't increase your investment
in Indonesia.

87
00:05:51,305 --> 00:05:53,990
Foreign markets aren't doing
as well as before.

88
00:05:53,992 --> 00:05:55,360
I'll handle it.

89
00:05:55,679 --> 00:05:58,264
- Then we'll be going...
- Excuse me.

90
00:05:59,332 --> 00:06:00,996
I heard your child is sick.

91
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,898
Does he really have cancer?

92
00:06:12,072 --> 00:06:13,827
They say he really has blood cancer.

93
00:06:14,012 --> 00:06:16,094
At this rate, there'll be one funeral
after another.

94
00:06:17,529 --> 00:06:20,870
- What?
- Now that I know it's true, I feel bad.

95
00:06:20,872 --> 00:06:23,558
I remember seeing him a few times
at the funeral.

96
00:06:24,118 --> 00:06:26,953
Why are you eating ramen
when there's rice?

97
00:06:27,547 --> 00:06:29,043
Did you put ice in it?

98
00:06:30,123 --> 00:06:31,919
Yeah. It's cold ramen.

99
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:33,653
It's refreshing.

100
00:06:36,878 --> 00:06:37,909
Is it serious?

101
00:06:39,097 --> 00:06:40,272
O Reum, I mean.

102
00:06:42,046 --> 00:06:44,740
Treatments are better these days,
so he'll be okay, right?

103
00:06:45,524 --> 00:06:46,885
We have to hope so.

104
00:07:57,972 --> 00:08:00,167
I have two hours until my appointment.

105
00:08:00,208 --> 00:08:02,277
I haven't practiced in days.
My hands feel stiff.

106
00:08:58,012 --> 00:09:00,116
I work part-time at a cafe.

107
00:09:00,118 --> 00:09:03,048
It's made with lots of fruit.

108
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:05,622
I wanted to bring you something,

109
00:09:05,875 --> 00:09:07,098
and...

110
00:09:08,525 --> 00:09:11,097
I wanted to see O Reum too.

111
00:09:11,345 --> 00:09:13,337
You didn't have to do this...

112
00:09:13,339 --> 00:09:14,818
Thank you.

113
00:09:15,512 --> 00:09:17,085
You probably hate me...

114
00:09:17,791 --> 00:09:19,511
That's between the adults.

115
00:09:20,572 --> 00:09:22,618
I was only thinking about O Reum.

116
00:09:23,178 --> 00:09:26,978
O Reum talks a lot
about his drawing friend too.

117
00:09:30,231 --> 00:09:32,531
- Flowers too.
- Want me to draw flowers?

118
00:09:33,722 --> 00:09:35,624
- A bird too.
- A bird too?

119
00:09:35,758 --> 00:09:38,198
How big should I make it?

120
00:09:40,425 --> 00:09:42,858
- And a rabbit.
- A rabbit too?

121
00:09:43,365 --> 00:09:44,529
What does a rabbit do?

122
00:09:44,531 --> 00:09:47,990
- It hops.
- A rabbit.

123
00:09:47,992 --> 00:09:49,864
Yes, a rabbit.

124
00:09:50,918 --> 00:09:55,413
- Mom and grandma too.
- Your mom and your grandma too?

125
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:58,571
Look. It's all done!

126
00:09:59,878 --> 00:10:02,957
I hate needles this big.

127
00:10:03,889 --> 00:10:05,405
That hurt, didn't it?

128
00:10:06,291 --> 00:10:08,491
I want to go home.

129
00:10:11,232 --> 00:10:16,118
- O Reum...
- I can't go home yet. I hate it here.

130
00:10:17,565 --> 00:10:18,808
I...

131
00:10:19,075 --> 00:10:21,658
hope you get better soon.

132
00:10:21,725 --> 00:10:23,281
Will you come back?

133
00:10:25,538 --> 00:10:26,801
If you...

134
00:10:27,352 --> 00:10:30,154
eat everything your mom gives you,

135
00:10:30,156 --> 00:10:31,494
and do your treatments.

136
00:10:31,687 --> 00:10:34,118
- I don't want to.
- What?

137
00:10:35,065 --> 00:10:39,383
- Then I can't come back.
- Okay. I will.

138
00:10:40,991 --> 00:10:42,088
Promise?

139
00:10:43,728 --> 00:10:44,835
Pinky swear?

140
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:47,605
Pinky swear.

141
00:10:50,392 --> 00:10:51,870
Want to draw again?

142
00:10:52,542 --> 00:10:53,854
What should I draw?

143
00:10:54,551 --> 00:10:56,640
She seems nice.

144
00:11:04,631 --> 00:11:07,016
Have some. It's really rich.

145
00:11:08,847 --> 00:11:09,858
Okay.

146
00:11:13,451 --> 00:11:14,899
Drink up.

147
00:11:15,432 --> 00:11:17,287
You need to take care of yourself.

148
00:11:18,150 --> 00:11:19,527
Mother,

149
00:11:20,478 --> 00:11:22,345
O Reum will get better soon, right?

150
00:11:24,132 --> 00:11:27,003
I can't stop thinking the worst.

151
00:11:27,694 --> 00:11:29,003
You have to believe.

152
00:11:29,452 --> 00:11:31,214
If you don't, who will?

153
00:11:31,649 --> 00:11:33,627
Believe. He'll be okay.

154
00:11:46,345 --> 00:11:47,767
Stay strong.

155
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:06,291
All this?

156
00:12:07,772 --> 00:12:11,765
- Now that's how rich people shop.
- We're not that rich.

157
00:12:12,218 --> 00:12:15,325
When he sets his heart on something,
he should buy plenty of it.

158
00:12:15,327 --> 00:12:17,031
"Plenty?"

159
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:19,868
I like that word.

160
00:12:21,192 --> 00:12:24,012
- How about some whiskey?
- Sure.

161
00:12:24,232 --> 00:12:25,691
I'll go lock the door.

162
00:12:35,632 --> 00:12:36,899
Cheers.

163
00:12:43,718 --> 00:12:48,349
I've got your dad backing me now.
I feel totally secure.

164
00:12:48,351 --> 00:12:51,261
My dad will never let you have your way.

165
00:12:51,379 --> 00:12:54,545
- You know how thorough he is.
- Who cares? That's later.

166
00:12:54,593 --> 00:12:57,233
Right now, I'm just happy.

167
00:12:57,457 --> 00:12:59,070
- Let's drink.
- Yeah.

168
00:13:06,592 --> 00:13:08,069
Feels like high school again.

169
00:13:08,738 --> 00:13:11,073
When I first drank with your dad
at your house,

170
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:13,058
- remember?
- Of course.

171
00:13:13,072 --> 00:13:14,990
You got drunk and said
you weren't going home,

172
00:13:14,992 --> 00:13:17,385
then you said it wasn't your house.
I was so confused.

173
00:13:17,832 --> 00:13:20,566
And your mom was glaring at me
from the side,

174
00:13:20,585 --> 00:13:21,723
you remember that?

175
00:13:21,725 --> 00:13:25,136
Like she was saying, "My son was fine
until he met the wrong friend."

176
00:13:25,278 --> 00:13:27,930
That exact look.
I was so unfairly blamed back then.

177
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:29,863
I really said it wasn't my house
back then too?

178
00:13:29,865 --> 00:13:31,531
That's your signature move.

179
00:13:31,611 --> 00:13:33,680
I seriously don't get it.

180
00:13:34,018 --> 00:13:35,592
Why do you keep saying
it's not your house?

181
00:13:35,645 --> 00:13:37,951
You have the strangest drunk habits.

182
00:13:42,371 --> 00:13:43,393
By the way,

183
00:13:44,347 --> 00:13:46,270
when are you marrying Do Hee?

184
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:48,843
It's still a long way off.
I just got back.

185
00:13:49,325 --> 00:13:50,996
After her exhibition is over
and her parents come.

186
00:13:50,998 --> 00:13:53,164
Is that exhibition even happening?

187
00:13:53,205 --> 00:13:55,678
- Have you seen her paintings?
- I have.

188
00:13:59,092 --> 00:14:00,701
You're being too hard on her.

189
00:14:00,952 --> 00:14:02,846
She's my fiancée. Show her some respect.

190
00:14:02,848 --> 00:14:04,301
Got it, you punk.

191
00:14:05,248 --> 00:14:07,434
You really do love her.

192
00:14:07,524 --> 00:14:09,820
For a cold-hearted guy like you,
you're surprisingly generous.

193
00:14:09,821 --> 00:14:11,687
You were so cold to Ji Ni.

194
00:14:11,689 --> 00:14:13,245
That's why I regret it.

195
00:14:13,848 --> 00:14:15,598
She said I have a habit
of making snap judgments.

196
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,362
Exactly. She was right about that.

197
00:14:17,605 --> 00:14:20,601
You said you started dating Do Hee
because you felt sorry for her.

198
00:14:20,612 --> 00:14:22,130
Intuition and snap judgments, huh?

199
00:14:22,132 --> 00:14:24,352
What was there to feel sorry for?
You completely misunderstood her.

200
00:14:24,396 --> 00:14:25,947
Can you really control your feelings?

201
00:14:28,008 --> 00:14:31,130
- I don't know.
- A man should always...

202
00:14:31,132 --> 00:14:32,642
watch out for pitiful women...

203
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,679
- and cute women.
- What about women?

204
00:14:36,604 --> 00:14:38,709
Someone worthy of her respect?

205
00:14:38,916 --> 00:14:41,039
I mean someone like me?

206
00:14:53,332 --> 00:14:54,758
I'll head out first.

207
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:57,726
- Okay. Good work today.
- See you.

208
00:15:01,196 --> 00:15:03,900
- I guess I'm your last patient.
- Yes.

209
00:15:04,084 --> 00:15:05,408
Can we have dinner?

210
00:15:05,452 --> 00:15:07,339
I was planning to eat with you.

211
00:15:08,344 --> 00:15:10,525
What do you want to eat? It's on me.

212
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:11,908
I think I'm going to make money.

213
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,388
Not that you made it already,
but you think you will?

214
00:15:15,388 --> 00:15:17,630
I told you I was going to become the CEO.

215
00:15:17,632 --> 00:15:20,184
I have a really good feeling
about the Indonesian investment.

216
00:15:20,188 --> 00:15:21,352
Really?

217
00:15:22,077 --> 00:15:25,270
Of course. You always had a good eye.

218
00:15:25,272 --> 00:15:26,396
Of course.

219
00:15:26,928 --> 00:15:29,870
So don't worry and tell me.
What should we eat?

220
00:15:30,885 --> 00:15:32,760
Sa Bin, you like sashimi, right?

221
00:15:37,612 --> 00:15:40,562
Are you really driving all the way
to the East Sea for sashimi?

222
00:15:40,564 --> 00:15:43,492
I want to treat you
to the freshest, best fish.

223
00:15:44,232 --> 00:15:46,988
I can't believe it's been so long
since I've driven like this.

224
00:15:47,036 --> 00:15:50,147
This is great, right?

225
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:52,785
Yes.

226
00:15:54,046 --> 00:15:55,668
What's with that reaction?

227
00:15:55,670 --> 00:15:57,588
Anyway, you've got incredible energy.

228
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:04,568
My energy and loyalty
are what keep me going.

229
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:06,821
- You know that.
- Yes.

230
00:16:07,612 --> 00:16:10,527
- Let me know if you're tired of driving.
- Okay.

231
00:16:28,294 --> 00:16:29,964
This is nice.

232
00:16:30,372 --> 00:16:33,743
I think the biggest dopamine rush
from a trip comes when you first leave.

233
00:16:34,016 --> 00:16:38,150
Once you arrive, same old routine.
Kind of boring, right?

234
00:16:38,209 --> 00:16:40,535
That's true, but I'm really enjoying this.

235
00:16:42,196 --> 00:16:44,636
- It's like watching a performance.
- "Performance?"

236
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:48,108
Your performances are always captivating
until the very end.

237
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:49,497
This feels exactly like that.

238
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:03,717
Think of him whenever he comes to mind.
Cry if you feel like crying.

239
00:17:03,804 --> 00:17:07,659
I can't tell my daughter not to cry
and then cry myself.

240
00:17:32,472 --> 00:17:35,844
Honey, I came to the ocean by myself.

241
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:37,768
By myself.

242
00:17:39,590 --> 00:17:42,980
You left on your own too,
so don't blame me.

243
00:17:57,892 --> 00:17:59,312
What are you thinking about?

244
00:18:01,236 --> 00:18:05,299
You have so many fans.
Why did you become friends with me?

245
00:18:05,796 --> 00:18:06,988
Why all of a sudden?

246
00:18:07,868 --> 00:18:09,920
I just started wondering.

247
00:18:10,732 --> 00:18:14,358
When I got in touch with you,
the musician I only watched on stage,

248
00:18:14,670 --> 00:18:16,315
I was so happy.

249
00:18:16,628 --> 00:18:17,933
Want to know?

250
00:18:18,912 --> 00:18:20,084
There's a reason?

251
00:18:23,988 --> 00:18:25,701
Because you're unattached.

252
00:18:26,288 --> 00:18:29,008
At our age, it's not easy
to find someone unattached.

253
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:32,607
Either they're seeing someone,
or they're divorced with kids.

254
00:18:33,356 --> 00:18:36,820
There's no one around you
who would pick a fight with me.

255
00:18:38,745 --> 00:18:40,734
I'm just kidding.

256
00:18:43,924 --> 00:18:45,460
It must've been really hard for you.

257
00:18:47,510 --> 00:18:49,940
I'm the one
who chose a difficult kind of love.

258
00:18:50,090 --> 00:18:53,226
My daughter says the same,
that it's the price I have to pay.

259
00:18:55,964 --> 00:19:00,187
I didn't know how to love him gently.

260
00:19:01,310 --> 00:19:05,604
Maybe he was hurting because of me too.

261
00:19:06,416 --> 00:19:08,158
I was so harsh on him.

262
00:19:10,370 --> 00:19:12,035
Please don't think like that.

263
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:22,368
Honey!

264
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,063
I'm sorry!

265
00:19:26,528 --> 00:19:28,192
Cha Min Ki!

266
00:19:29,052 --> 00:19:30,516
I'm sorry.

267
00:19:34,901 --> 00:19:36,133
I'm sorry.

268
00:19:42,112 --> 00:19:44,732
I hope you're not hurting anymore.

269
00:19:47,596 --> 00:19:48,988
I'm sorry.

270
00:20:09,372 --> 00:20:12,354
- Grandma, what are you doing?
- What?

271
00:20:13,008 --> 00:20:17,287
- O Reum, you're not asleep?
- Yeah, I can't sleep.

272
00:20:17,972 --> 00:20:22,065
- You still need to sleep.
- Am I getting treated tomorrow?

273
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:23,676
Right.

274
00:20:31,604 --> 00:20:35,510
I asked what you were doing.

275
00:20:37,228 --> 00:20:43,378
My student sent me some photos,
so I was looking at them.

276
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:48,403
The one who sent
the herbal medicine last time.

277
00:20:48,661 --> 00:20:50,555
It's the sea.

278
00:20:51,368 --> 00:20:54,662
Once you get better,
shall we go see the sea too?

279
00:20:54,664 --> 00:20:57,262
Yeah, I'd love that.

280
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:01,124
Then you should hurry and sleep.
Close your eyes tight.

281
00:21:02,116 --> 00:21:03,516
That's it.

282
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:17,468
You must be in the hospital room.

283
00:21:17,878 --> 00:21:20,481
Take a breather
while looking at the sea photos.

284
00:21:24,693 --> 00:21:26,321
(Singing Teacher)

285
00:21:26,323 --> 00:21:29,489
Thank you. You went quite far.

286
00:21:32,630 --> 00:21:35,320
The person I once told you about,
who went through something sad,

287
00:21:35,321 --> 00:21:36,920
wanted to see the sea, so I came.

288
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:42,622
You must be an angel
who only does good for others.

289
00:21:45,170 --> 00:21:46,299
No, not at all.

290
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:49,739
Even if you don't have an appetite,
make sure to eat and get plenty of rest.

291
00:22:02,916 --> 00:22:07,525
You too, Sa Bin.
Travel back to Seoul safely.

292
00:23:17,716 --> 00:23:19,082
Get some more rest.

293
00:23:19,295 --> 00:23:21,402
No, I'm awake now.

294
00:23:23,044 --> 00:23:24,295
Would you like some coffee?

295
00:23:26,628 --> 00:23:30,501
- Let's get to Seoul before traffic.
- Okay.

296
00:23:34,984 --> 00:23:38,089
An overnight stay, finally.

297
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:42,148
Father, Mother,
the day you've been waiting for has come.

298
00:23:48,230 --> 00:23:49,732
My goodness!

299
00:23:50,372 --> 00:23:53,448
- You really came all the way here?
- Who is she? Is the wedding this fall?

300
00:23:53,450 --> 00:23:55,116
- Are you finally getting married?
- Come on!

301
00:23:55,176 --> 00:23:57,880
Why jump the gun all night?
You must've had your fill.

302
00:23:57,950 --> 00:24:00,686
- It's not what you think!
- Staying out overnight? That makes sense?

303
00:24:00,688 --> 00:24:02,487
That's really not it.

304
00:24:03,008 --> 00:24:05,915
I got drunk and came back at dawn.

305
00:24:05,917 --> 00:24:06,981
Sure, you were drunk.

306
00:24:06,982 --> 00:24:09,764
Who ever made history while sober?

307
00:24:09,977 --> 00:24:12,531
Please leave.
I need to wash up and go to work.

308
00:24:13,484 --> 00:24:15,457
Let's print the wedding invitations, okay?

309
00:24:15,652 --> 00:24:18,224
No, it's not like that.

310
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:20,894
- Print the invitations.
- It's really not necessary.

311
00:24:22,556 --> 00:24:24,258
I knew I shouldn't have come in.

312
00:24:24,260 --> 00:24:26,300
I should just move out again or something.

313
00:24:26,390 --> 00:24:28,239
He never stops talking.

314
00:24:41,056 --> 00:24:43,728
What? Why? Need some money?

315
00:24:43,730 --> 00:24:45,168
Can I stay out overnight too?

316
00:24:45,170 --> 00:24:47,078
Like mother, like daughter, right?

317
00:24:47,796 --> 00:24:50,780
I went to see the sea, got drunk,
and just dozed off for a bit.

318
00:24:50,836 --> 00:24:52,410
You nag about everything.

319
00:24:52,556 --> 00:24:54,890
I'm a widow. I'm free.

320
00:24:54,892 --> 00:24:58,944
I'll keep you in line
more than your husband did.

321
00:24:59,090 --> 00:25:00,888
Dad let everything slide until now.

322
00:25:00,890 --> 00:25:03,589
- I won't.
- So scary.

323
00:25:03,852 --> 00:25:05,425
Mind your own business.

324
00:25:13,300 --> 00:25:14,748
This is so annoying.

325
00:25:14,749 --> 00:25:17,240
Your dad used to do all this stuff.

326
00:25:17,597 --> 00:25:21,138
He promised he'd take care of it forever.
How could he leave first?

327
00:25:21,140 --> 00:25:22,908
Did you keep a husband or a servant?

328
00:25:22,910 --> 00:25:24,260
You made him do everything.

329
00:25:24,261 --> 00:25:26,765
He even said he'd always pour my wine.

330
00:25:27,152 --> 00:25:29,800
He promised I'd never
have to pour my own drinks again.

331
00:25:29,802 --> 00:25:33,253
Dad sure made a lot of pointless promises.

332
00:25:33,716 --> 00:25:36,632
So who did you drink with yesterday?

333
00:25:36,633 --> 00:25:38,326
Where did you drink?

334
00:25:39,888 --> 00:25:41,748
Why couldn't you come home?

335
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:44,184
Dad hasn't been gone long,
and you're already staying out all night?

336
00:25:44,256 --> 00:25:47,472
- Say one more word, I dare you.
- Answer me.

337
00:25:47,836 --> 00:25:50,563
The Korean medicine doctor.
You saw him too, right?

338
00:25:50,820 --> 00:25:53,246
I went for acupuncture,
and dinner just ran long.

339
00:25:53,248 --> 00:25:56,062
- It sure ran long.
- I called you.

340
00:25:56,064 --> 00:25:58,988
- You didn't answer, so stop acting up.
- My phone was on silent.

341
00:25:59,032 --> 00:26:01,143
I set it to silent in the evening
and forgot about it.

342
00:26:01,252 --> 00:26:04,026
What about you? What were you hiding
that you had it on silent?

343
00:26:06,488 --> 00:26:09,262
I went to the hospital yesterday.
I wanted to see O Reum.

344
00:26:09,264 --> 00:26:10,902
I guess I left it
on silent then and forgot.

345
00:26:11,060 --> 00:26:13,188
Why would you go to that awful household?

346
00:26:13,190 --> 00:26:16,604
Even after they chased you
all the way here, you're not furious?

347
00:26:17,064 --> 00:26:20,498
- Sick or dying, stay out of it!
- Mom.

348
00:26:20,500 --> 00:26:23,510
- O Reum didn't do anything wrong.
- What about you?

349
00:26:23,512 --> 00:26:26,528
What did you do to deserve all that abuse?

350
00:26:27,128 --> 00:26:28,788
No Yeong Ju.

351
00:26:28,790 --> 00:26:32,877
Do you know what kind of curse
she put on you when you were a newborn?

352
00:26:33,050 --> 00:26:34,895
I don't even want to repeat it.

353
00:26:35,092 --> 00:26:38,028
Why do you think I'm so obsessed
with your marriage?

354
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:40,410
Because I want to break that curse.

355
00:26:40,420 --> 00:26:41,880
But just because...

356
00:26:41,936 --> 00:26:44,354
her grandson is sick,
you went to that woman's place?

357
00:26:46,046 --> 00:26:47,914
- You have no pride at all.
- Mom.

358
00:26:47,980 --> 00:26:49,480
Are you not my daughter?

359
00:26:49,481 --> 00:26:51,901
If she's my enemy,
then she should be your enemy too.

360
00:26:55,553 --> 00:26:59,660
If I was wronged as you say,
then O Reum was wronged too.

361
00:26:59,810 --> 00:27:02,696
He's just a sick child. Like me.

362
00:27:02,750 --> 00:27:04,587
If you got insulted because of me,

363
00:27:04,588 --> 00:27:07,368
then O Reum is suffering
because of his own mom and grandmother.

364
00:27:07,370 --> 00:27:09,222
That's not something you should pity.

365
00:27:12,360 --> 00:27:14,254
Try going there one more time,

366
00:27:14,256 --> 00:27:16,209
- and I'll break your legs.
- Mom!

367
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:19,304
Do you have that much free time?
Is there no end to your sympathy?

368
00:27:19,428 --> 00:27:22,367
Even so, you can't do that.
You absolutely can't!

369
00:27:52,810 --> 00:27:55,976
(Family Register)

370
00:27:56,072 --> 00:27:58,752
- You shouldn't be acting like this.
- I keep getting anxious thoughts.

371
00:27:58,796 --> 00:28:01,572
Everyone wants to protect
the people they love.

372
00:28:01,612 --> 00:28:03,872
- I wish you'd just stay out of it.
- Mother.

373
00:28:03,915 --> 00:28:05,692
Mom, you're really making me
feel miserable.

374
00:28:05,709 --> 00:28:07,396
You're the one who made me like this.

375
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:08,724
Are you worse than your own daughter?

376
00:28:08,756 --> 00:28:10,876
Is that woman Father mentioned
really Ji Ni?

377
00:28:10,920 --> 00:28:12,940
- You passed.
- Did you get close to Director Ji Hu?

378
00:28:13,020 --> 00:28:14,032
Yeah, a bit.

379
00:28:14,049 --> 00:28:16,164
- Can I say it?
- Yes.

380
00:28:17,497 --> 00:28:19,497
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
